# Onboarding tour

Full write-up: `docs/onboarding-tour/README.md`.

## Shape (23 steps in four parts)
- **Main Menu (5)** — `TourProgress.menuSteps`: welcome, startButton,
  soloMode ("Two Ways to Play": Solo + Combat cards), instantStart,
  leaderboard ("More to Explore": Top Score + Settings + About). Driven by
  skeleton_core's `TourBloc`, rendered by `GlobalTourWrapper`.
- **Regular (8) / Pick Right (5) / Combat (5)** — `TutorialScript.lessons`,
  driven by `TutorialCubit`, rendered by `TutorialOverlay` (mounted last in
  the `Stack` of PlayScreen, GameOverScreen, CombatPlayScreen,
  CombatGameEndScreen). The whole practice is the single tour slot
  `TourStep.gameTutorialStep1`.
- Progress labels come only from `TourProgress.menuLabel` / `lessonLabel`
  ("Main Menu · 2 / 5", "Regular · 3 / 8"). Never use skeleton_core's
  `totalSteps` / `displayStepNumber` (they count unused enum values).

## Rules
- **Menu navigation**: Next / Previous use `TourJumpToStep` with
  `TourProgress.nextAfter` / `previousBefore` (list order, not enum order).
  Never `TourStepCompleted()` / `TourStepBack()`.
- **One look**: both parts render `TourSpotlightLayer` + `TourCard`
  (`widgets/tour_card.dart`) — same AlertTemplate-style card, same dimmed
  spotlight. Don't build a separate dialog/tooltip.
- **Highlight targets** are `GlobalKey`s in `TourKeys`, measured with
  `getRectForKeys` (which skips elements on a covered route). A new target
  needs: a key in `TourKeys` (+ `reset()`), the key on the widget, a
  `TutorialSpotlight` value and a case in `TutorialOverlay._targetRect`
  (or `GlobalTourWrapper._targetKeysForStep` for menu steps).
- **Result cards shown on another screen** (a timeout/win that ends the
  game) must point at that screen: `gameOverSummary`
  (GameOverScreen), `combatResult` (CombatGameEndScreen) — not at the hidden
  game screen's panels.
- **Seeds**: a lesson with `turnSeed` / `combatSeed` sets the real game up
  when `seedToken` changes. A lesson without one continues the previous
  lesson's real state — only valid when reached with Next.
  `TutorialCubit.previous()` lands on the nearest seeded lesson
  (`previousSeededIndex`), so Previous never shows another lesson's data.
  Previous on the first lesson calls `backToMenuTour()` (ends the practice,
  `backedOutToMenuTour: true`, does NOT complete the tour).
- **Host screens**: `PlayerNav` / `CombatNav` move between PlayScreen ⇄
  GameOverScreen and CombatPlayScreen ⇄ CombatGameEndScreen when the lesson's
  `hostScreen` changes, including on a re-seed while the end screen shows.
- **Card placement** (`TourCardPlacement`) keeps the card inside one pane on
  a hinged device, beside the target (landscape) or above/below (portrait),
  scrolling only the description so title and buttons stay visible. The
  spotlight re-measures for 800 ms after every change (page slides, scrolls,
  fold/unfold) in its own coordinates.
- **Text**: titles/descriptions via `AppLocalizations`; `**bold**` and `\n`
  (one paragraph per point) are supported. Menu strings are translated;
  `tourRule*` lesson strings are English in every locale.
- The optional app-update prompt waits for the tour to finish
  (`UpdateCheckerWrapper`); a forced update shows immediately.
- After any tour change run `integration_test/tour_guide_test.dart` — it
  walks every step forwards and back and checks title, label, layout,
  highlight and seeded data, driven by `TutorialScript` itself.
